  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_fold_cb688279e41c60b45a8ec68b885ab1402d7a80de49f7a56ae59d4751517965e40f">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>a wrapping, covering (OED fold n.3 3), however this clearly has something to do with armor, here with mail (Cobb 179 'faulds, skirts of metal hoops' cross-referencing aprons, mail) | a wrapping, covering (OED fold n.3 3), however this clearly has something to do with armour (usually together with flankers) | a wrapping, covering (OED s.v. fold n.3 3), however this clearly has something to do with armour (usually together with flankers) | a wrapping, covering (OED s.v. fold n.3 (3)), however this clearly has something to do with armor (here imported together with gussettes) | some kind of armor, but exact meaning unknown | fold is a wrapping, covering (OED fold n.3 3), however this clearly has something to do with armor, here with mail (Cobb 179 'faulds, skirts of metal hoops' cross-referencing aprons, mail)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
